# The host throws, the guest catches: the guest takes a body it only ever saw as a copy, so it
# continues from the receiver's estimate of its velocity. Measured, not judged, beyond rest.
scenario throw_catch
scene two_chars_item
seed 17
guests 1
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%

p0 walk box
p0 grab box as lift
p0 wait 300ms
p0 throw 1.6 0.6 0.4 speed 5 as throw
at 550ms p1 walk box speed 4
p1 grab box as catch
p1 wait 500ms
p1 drop as put

expect result lift granted
expect result throw done
expect result catch granted
expect agree_at_rest 5cm
expect no_stuck
# Derived: a copy's visible correction in a tick (its drawn move less its owner's at the same
# event time, or less its own step for a predicted copy) is at most a render offset's release,
# 0.15 of at most 2 m: 0.3 m. A placement the offset does not take shows as its whole move.
expect jump.max <= 0.3m
